find -name filename.txt
grep "text" filename.ext
grep -R "text" /folder
file filename ... determines the filetype
su user2 ... stays in our home directory
su -l user2  ... takes to the user2 home directory

rwx 421

/etc - system files of OS ... passwd, shadow, sudoers
/var - files which are frequently accessed/written by services or applications and other data not necessarily
associated with a specific user... e.g. /var/log , 
/root - home directory of the root user

/tmp - any user has access to this folder - contents are cleared once the system restarts
Nano - ctrl+6 , alt+6, alt + u -- select text, copy text and paste text

wget "Filepath" - for downloading the file
scp file_to_be_copied user@remoteip:destination/filename
scp user@remoteip:source_with_file filename

to convert into a web server for sharing files  - python3 -m http.server
wget http://10.129.162.81:8000/myfile - the http server runs on port 8000

